    {
      "section": "Mathematics",
      "text": "If ω is a complex cube root of unity, then the value of (1 - ω + ω^2)(1 + ω - ω^2) is:",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "0",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "1",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "4",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "-4",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "Shortcut: Use 1+ω+ω^2=0 ⇒ 1+ω^2=-ω and 1+ω=-ω^2. First bracket = -ω-ω = -2ω. Second bracket = -ω^2-ω^2 = -2ω^2. Product = 4ω^3 = 4. Full Solution: Since ω is a cube root of unity, 1+ω+ω^2=0 and ω^3=1. Then 1+ω^2 = -ω, so (1-ω+ω^2) = -ω-ω = -2ω. Similarly, 1+ω = -ω^2, so (1+ω-ω^2) = -ω^2-ω^2 = -2ω^2. Multiplying: (-2ω)(-2ω^2) = 4ω^3 = 4(1) = 4.",
